                  {
                     "text" : "\tmaybe “SafeSequence<",
                     "type" : "text"
                  },
                  {
                     "type" : "hardBreak"
                  },
                  {
                     "text" : "“SafeSequence<> “ : Sequence<> - and that mimics each API and assignemt. For ALL – its thressafe rep. But SafeSequence (and SafeXXX for each subclass) – does envelope threasasafety. A bit like my experimental Contianer::Optional<> code.",
                     "type" : "text"
                  },
                  {
                     "type" : "hardBreak"
                  },
                  {
                     "text" : "o\tThen – ASSIGNEMNTs all work for data mebers (they are all safe) – but the args to functions aren’t and don’t pay costs!!!",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            }
